  "catalog": {
    "slug": "farmers-market",
    "title": "Farmers Market Saturday",
    "version": "0.1.0",
    "author": "simetro",
    "description": "Stalls open at sunrise. Stock the booth from the back truck, watch the apricots before the noon sun softens them, and time the bakery delivery so the croissants are still warm at peak foot traffic.",
    "tags": [
      "sl1",
      "scenario_language_v1",
      "showcase",
      "daily_life",
      "easy"
    ],
    "palette_note": "Lemon-yellow awning over slate cobblestones; tomato red for ripe stock, marigold for the bakery box, basil green for produce, sky blue for the bag-your-own bins, eggplant for the busker.",
    "layout_note": "Back-of-truck (source) restocks the stall (compute_cluster), shoppers pay at the front register (dashboard), and a roving market manager (operator) keeps an eye on the aisles.",
    "node_language_note": "source / compute_cluster / dashboard / operator. The compute_cluster is the stall itself \u2014 boxes are unpacked, sorted, and arranged here.",
    "mover_path_note": "Movers do not exist yet for SL1 scenes; the legacy pieces.movers array is intentionally empty. SL1 links from back-truck to stall to register represent typed produce-to-receipt flow; pack-shopper-bag runs on stall and ring-up-sale on register, with the market-mgr overlay watching via walkie. The SL1 renderer will translate links into visible carts.",
    "review_note": "Marked status=draft in the frontend catalog because the SL1 canvas renderer is not yet wired. Selecting this scene loads it successfully and shows catalog metadata in the scene browser. The SL1 HUD chips, dashboard freshness pill, and milestone strip render via the existing SL1 HUD overlay; the bespoke canvas vignette ships when the SL1 renderer is wired in a later PR."
  },
